## Submit (private GitHub repository)

How to submit:
- Push the repo to a **private** GitHub repository (not public).
- Share it with **Maxim Naydenko**, GitHub user **`naymax-szl`**.
- Send the repo link through the **submission link in the separate email**.
- Deadline: **within 7 business days of receiving the task, end of day your time.**

`TASK.md` requires the logs to be part of the submission: the full git history (not squashed), the terminal recordings, and the complete, unedited AI assistant logs. With a repo as the submission, they go into a `logs/` folder inside it, in one last commit after the recording has stopped.

### S1. Stop the agent and the recording

If you used Claude Code, exit it first with `/exit`, so its log is complete. Then stop the recording:

```bash
exit                                   # ends script; timing.log and session.log are now complete
cd ~/work/finding-relay
```

### S2. Copy the logs into the repo

```bash
mkdir -p logs/terminal logs/claude-code logs/claude-chat

# terminal recordings (all sittings)
cp ../timing*.log ../session*.log logs/terminal/

# Claude Code: every project folder it wrote (the .jsonl files AND the <session-id>/ folders)
ls ~/.claude/projects/ 2>/dev/null       # look for folders containing "finding-relay" or "work"
cp -r ~/.claude/projects/*finding-relay* logs/claude-code/ 2>/dev/null || true
cp -r ~/.claude/projects/*-work logs/claude-code/ 2>/dev/null || true
ls -R logs/claude-code | head -20        # expect <session-id>.jsonl and a <session-id>/ folder per session
```

If you started Claude Code from any other folder, also copy that folder's entry under `~/.claude/projects/`. If you did not use Claude Code, remove the empty folder: `rmdir logs/claude-code`.

**This chat (claude.ai), where the guide was prepared:**
1. In claude.ai, open this conversation and use **Share** to create a link; copy it.
2. Save a copy: with the conversation open, press **Ctrl+P** and choose **Save as PDF**. Scroll to the top first so the whole chat is loaded. Name it `claude-chat.pdf` and save it in `C:\Users\USER\Downloads\assessment_setup`.
3. Then:

```bash
cp ~/work/assessment_setup/claude-chat.pdf logs/claude-chat/
```

Write the index file (fill in the share link):

```bash
cat > logs/README.md <<'EOF'
# Logs

- `terminal/`: terminal recordings of every working session (`script -T`).
  Replay: `scriptreplay -t terminal/timing.log terminal/session.log`
- `claude-code/`: complete, unedited Claude Code session logs copied from
  `~/.claude/projects/` (each `<session-id>.jsonl` with its `<session-id>/`
  folder: subagents and tool-results).
- `claude-chat/`: the claude.ai conversation used to analyse the task and
  prepare the changes. Share link: <PASTE-SHARE-LINK-HERE>

Redactions, if any, are marked [REDACTED-BY-CANDIDATE].
EOF
```

Check for anything private before you commit: tokens, passwords, personal content unrelated to the task. Recordings capture what was printed, but `sudo` passwords are never echoed. Anything you remove must be replaced with `[REDACTED-BY-CANDIDATE]`.

```bash
grep -rIl -E "ghp_|github_pat_|sk-ant-|password=" logs/ || echo "nothing obvious found"
git add logs
git commit -m "Add terminal recordings and assistant session logs"
git log --oneline | head -15            # kit history, your 11 commits, then the logs commit
```

### S3. Create the private repo and push

Install and sign in to the GitHub CLI (one time; the login opens your browser):

```bash
sudo apt install -y gh
gh auth login            # GitHub.com > HTTPS > Login with a web browser; enter the code shown
```

Create the **private** repo from this folder and push all history:

```bash
cd ~/work/finding-relay
gh repo create finding-relay --private --source=. --remote=origin --push
git push origin --all
gh repo view --json visibility,url       # must say "PRIVATE"
```

If a repo called `finding-relay` already exists in your account, use another name, e.g. `finding-relay-assessment`.

### S4. Share it with Maxim Naydenko

```bash
gh api -X PUT "repos/$(gh api user --jq .login)/finding-relay/collaborators/naymax-szl" -f permission=pull
