## Troubleshooting on Windows

| Problem | Fix |
|---|---|
| `docker: command not found` in Ubuntu | Docker Desktop → Settings → Resources → WSL integration → enable Ubuntu-24.04 |
| `Cannot connect to the Docker daemon` | Docker Desktop isn't running; start it and wait for "Engine running" |
| `make up` times out waiting for a URL | a port is taken (see Prerequisites §5), or Docker is still starting; `make down` and retry |
| `go test -race` says `cgo` / `gcc not found` | `sudo apt install -y build-essential` |
| `gofmt` or the diff shows every line changed | the file got CRLF endings; in VS Code click **CRLF** in the status bar → **LF**, save |
| `gh repo create` says the name exists | use another name and replace `finding-relay` in S3/S4 |
| `git push` asks for a password | run `gh auth login` again and choose HTTPS; `gh auth setup-git` |
| `unzip` asks for a password on packet 2 | use the `-P second-packet-7Hq2vX` command exactly as in step 6 |
| Slow builds | the repo is under `/mnt/c` (for example inside `assessment_setup`); work in `~/work` instead |

